<Base title="What This Is" description="What enragecolorado.org is, what it is not, and how to add to the record.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">What this is</p>
    <h1 class="display" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.2rem); margin: 0.4rem 0 1rem;">
      A standing answer, kept by the public.
    </h1>

    <p>
      <strong>enragecolorado.org</strong> is a work of political satire, parody, and commentary. The name
      is a play on words. The purpose is serious: to keep a durable, public counter-record to the
      self-congratulatory stories that powerful people tell about their own politics — here, the strand
      of techno-authoritarian, venture-funded political power as it shows up in Colorado.
    </p>

    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An independent, volunteer-kept monument. It is meant to be added to for years, not posted once.</li>
      <li>Original commentary and satire. We write our own words about public matters; we do not reprint anyone else's site.</li>
      <li>Opinion and rhetorical hyperbole, offered as what it is — argument in the public square.</li>
      <li>Open source. Every entry is a markdown file. Anyone can propose one, correct one, or argue with one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Not affiliated</strong> with, endorsed by, or connected to any organization, campaign, fund,
        or person it responds to — including any entity with a similar-sounding name. Any resemblance is the
        point of the parody, not a claim of association.
      </li>
      <li>Not a copy of anyone's content. It is a response to ideas, not a reproduction of pages.</li>
      <li>Not a dossier on private individuals. We criticize public conduct, public money, and public ideology — not people's private lives — and nothing here is offered as a statement of fact about any identifiable private person.</li>
      <li>Not legal, financial, or voting advice.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The one idea</h2>
    <p>
      When software can manufacture consent as cheaply as it manufactures anything else, the people with the
      most capital get to write the "honest assessment" of what just happened — and then treat their own
      comfort as the neutral truth. This site exists so that assessment is not the <em>only</em> one on the
      record. The public gets a pen too.
    </p>

    <h2>Add to the record</h2>
    <p>
      The monument grows by contribution. Open a pull request with a new markdown file in
      <code>src/content/assessments/</code>, or open an issue with a claim, a source, or a correction.
      Bring receipts; we would rather be accurate than loud.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/ahoward/enragecolorado">github.com/ahoward/enragecolorado →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
